  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Bento Grid**\n\nI\'m digging into the \"Bento Grid\" design theme and examining the provided HTML. I\'m focusing on the structural elements and how they implement the Bento Grid concept. Initial observations point towards a column-based layout with a distinct aesthetic. I\'m noting the use of specific dimensions, colors, and fonts as they relate to this grid style.\n\n\n**Examining Uptime Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on the HTML for the \"uptime\" and \"daily budget\" display. The code uses flexbox for layout within the header and a simple text alignment. I am noting the use of specific text sizes, font families (mono), and color choices to see how they fit into the overall design language. The components appear to be well-structured with clear semantic meaning. I will check for any specific use of classes to understand the styling more in-depth.\n\n\n**Detailing Component Styles**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the styling attributes for each Bento card. I\'ve noted the `bg-[#18181b]`, `border border-[#27272a]`, `rounded-3xl`, and `p-6` (or `p-5`) patterns consistently applied. I\'m focusing on how these combine for the visual effect, and I\'m correlating this with the `col-span` and `row-span` values to reconstruct the grid layout. The elements are using a consistent background, border and padding style, with varied grid dimensions.\n\n\n**Defining Design Guidelines**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the Bento Grid design, specifically the color scheme. I\'ve broken down the palette into distinct elements: background, containers, insets, and primary/secondary accents (Indigo, Emerald, Amber). I\'m noting specific color codes and their associated styles, such as text colors and glow effects. The consistent use of zinc-50 and zinc-400 for text is also interesting. I\'ve also examined the text tracking, specifically the use of uppercase text.\n\n\n**Refining Style Definitions**\n\nI\'m now detailing the component styling, noting the use of varied border radii: from `rounded-3xl` for Bento containers down to `rounded-md` or `rounded-full` for indicator pills. I\'m taking notes of the subtle, consistent border styles and how they are used for indicators. The Bento grid layout\'s modular compartmentalization is also clearer now. I\'ve got a grasp of the color palette, and I am mapping this onto specific visual hierarchy elements. I\'ve also identified specific style changes for `App.tsx` and `Header.tsx`.\n\n\n**Defining Component Styles**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific component styling updates. I\'ve noted the updated styling for the indigo icon square, with its subtle glow. I\'ve also identified specific style changes for the uptime and daily budget indicators, including the use of `font-mono` and color modifications. I\'ve documented changes to navigation tabs, including active and inactive states. Finally, I\'ve checked the 10-Stage Pipeline card styling updates.\n\n\n**Summarizing Visual Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing updates in the bento blocks, noting the `#09090b` backgrounds, `#27272a` borders, and indigo active glows for the 10-stage items. I\'ve broken down styling for the main area, including the fleet status tiles, job queue card (with progress indicators) and the job details bento card. I\'ve also checked out the HITL approval queue card and stage/asset tab styling. The TelegramSimulator component gets the Bento treatment too!\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 561720000
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
