  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the UI Design**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started examining the uploaded screenshot and focusing on the UI design. I\'m carefully parsing the top navigation bar. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the left side, noting the four-squares grid icon and the green lightning bolt icon alongside the \"CONTENT-FACTORY\" text. I\'m trying to identify the specific elements and infer their function.\n\n\n**Evaluating Navigation Elements**\n\nOkay, I\'ve just started to go deeper on the UI navigation, specifically that dark, rounded pill container for the navigation tabs. I\'m noting the \'Pipeline\' tab is active, contrasting with \'Analytics\' and \'Style Guides\'. Also considering options like adding \'Telegram HITL\', \'Agents\', and \'Codebase\' into these tabs. Then, I\'m analyzing the right-side elements, including the \"Connected\" pill and the settings/moon icons. Finally, evaluating a \'+ New Pipeline\' button.\n\n\n**Mapping Agent Functionality**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how agents are presented within the interface. I\'m focusing on the agent name, status indicators (like active/ready dots), and category badges (teal, pink, yellow). The goal is to make it super clear what an agent does by adding short descriptions and model badges, with the ability to inspect an agent in detail! I\'m also planning the connection of the node graphs.\n\n**Visualizing Workflow Nodes**\n\nI\'ve moved on to designing the workflow canvas with its node graph. It\'ll have a dot grid background, similar to n8n or React Flow. I\'m aiming for three rows of nodes arranged in an S-curve to represent the workflow, starting with an \'IDEA\' node (lightbulb icon) that\'s connected to \'RESEARCH\' node (search icon) and then a \'SCRIPT\' node. I plan to highlight completed stages.\n\n\n**Defining Node Visualizations**\n\nI\'m now detailing the visual aspects of each workflow node, specifically, the appearance of the `SCRIPT`, `QC1`, and other nodes, focusing on their icons, labels, and color-coded borders. I\'m assigning icons like `FileText`, `CheckSquare`, `Palette`, and `Image`, and indicating connector line directions. I\'m also describing the rounded rectangular design and connector handles of each node. I\'m focusing on how the amber glowing border will indicate the currently active stage!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 525012495
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
