le positions and created the corresponding `M` and `L` coordinates for each line segment, precisely matching the screenshot layout and node coordinates.\n\n\n**Determining Node Status**\n\nI\'m now determining each node\'s status based on the selected job, to be mapped to the dashboard. If a stage precedes the current stage, or if the job is completed, it\'s marked as \"completed\" with a green visual cue. Conversely, the current active stage receives an amber/orange \"active\" designation based on its particular status.\n\n\n**Defining Node Statuses**\n\nI\'m now implementing the different node states (\"completed\", \"active\", \"pending\"), including color-coding (green, amber/orange, dark slate) and status dots. I\'m focusing on the connection line styling, specifying green for connections between completed nodes, amber for those leading to an active node (animated dot!), and muted slate for connections between pending nodes.\n\nI\'ve also begun examining the left sidebar, starting with the header (\"AGENTS\" with a robot icon). I\'m looking at the list of agents: Manager, Researcher, Scriptwriter and Style Analyst, including their respective descriptions, models and icons.\n\n\n**Implementing Agent Sidebar**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the left sidebar implementation. I\'ve successfully defined a list of agents, each with a green status dot and relevant details. I\'m focusing on the click interaction and how it highlights the corresponding node on the workflow canvas. I\'m also preparing to integrate a detail drawer for each agent, displaying its associated prompts, tools, and schemas.\n\nI\'ve also started working on the top bar in the screenshot, specifically the left side, by implementing the 4-squares grid icon and the \"CONTENT-FACTORY\" label. I\'m now looking at implementing the pill navigation on the top bar. I\'m planning out the visual style and functionality of the pills: \"Pipeline,\" \"Analytics,\" and \"Style Guides\".\n\n\n"
