  planner_response {
    response: "I have re-architected the frontend into a **node-based workflow canvas dashboard**, matching the layout, visual structure, and interactive flow:\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural & Visual Implementations\n\n- **Top Navigation Bar**:\n  - **Brand & Menu**: Integrated the 4-square grid app drawer trigger alongside the green electric bolt badge and uppercase `CONTENT-FACTORY` branding.\n  - **Pill Navigation Tabs**: Replaced the previous layout with the centralized n8n pill tabs (**Pipeline**, **Analytics**, **Style Guides**, **Telegram HITL**, and **Codebase**).\n  - **Live Indicator & Controls**: Embedded the `\342\227\217 Connected` green pill indicator, quick settings drawer, dark mode toggle, and a **+ New Job** pipeline creator.\n\n- **Left Sidebar (\"AGENTS\")**:\n  - **Agent Fleet Dossiers**: Styled all 9 autonomous agents (**Manager**, **Researcher**, **Scriptwriter**, **Style Analyst**, **Art Director**, **Video Editor**, **Quality Control**, **Poster**, and **Analyst**) in collapsible cards.\n  - **Sub-Roles & Engine Badges**: Each agent displays their specific division (`ORCHESTRATION`, `RESEARCH OPS`, `CREATIVE`, `VISUAL INTEL`, `ASSEMBLY`, `AUDIT & SAFETY`, `DISTRIBUTION`, `PERFORMANCE`), status dots, and assigned engine badges (`gemini-3.6-flash`, `gemini-3.6-pro`, `ffmpeg + veo`, `postiz-api`).\n  - **Interactive Node Focusing**: Clicking any agent in the sidebar immediately centers and selects the corresponding stage on the canvas.\n\n- **Serpentine Workflow Canvas (11 Interactive Nodes)**:\n  - **Dot Matrix Grid Canvas**: Implemented a deep `#0a0f1d` canvas with custom 24px dot-matrix background styling.\n  - **Geometric 3-Row Node Layout**:\n    - **Row 1 (Left \342\236\224 Right)**: `IDEA` \342\236\224 `RESEARCH` \342\236\224 `SCRIPT` \342\236\224 `QC1`\n    - **Row 2 (Right \360\237\240\224 Left)**: `STYLE` \360\237\240\224 `ART` \360\237\240\224 `VIDEO` \360\237\240\224 `AWAITING_PREMIUM`\n    - **Row 3 (Left \342\236\224 Right)**: `QC2` \342\236\224 `POST` \342\236\224 `ANALYZE`\n  - **Node Aesthetics**: Each node is enclosed in a dark slate container with 4 border connection handles (top, bottom, left, right), an upper-right status dot, large centered stage icons, and stage titles.\n  - **Dynamic SVG Connection Cables**:\n    - **Completed Connections**: Glowing emerald wires (`#10b981`).\n    - **Active Execution Connection**: Amber wire (`#f59e0b`) featuring an animated SVG particle moving along the path.\n    - **Pending Connections**: Dark slate wires (`#283952`).\n  - **Pan & Zoom Interaction**: Full drag-to-pan canvas navigation, zoom in (`+`), zoom out (`\342\210\222`), reset to fit (`\342\233\266`), and canvas lock (`\360\237\224\222`).\n  - **Bottom-Right Mini-Map**: Embedded an interactive mini-map with active viewport bounds tracking and the watermark badge.\n\n- **Right Slide-Out Node Inspector**:\n  - Clicking any node opens a slide-out drawer displaying the stage\'s real-time output payload, token counts, engine details, and execution triggers.\n  - **HITL Gate Controls**: For approval gates (`SCRIPT`, `QC1`, `AWAITING_PREMIUM`, `QC2`), users can directly trigger **Approve Gate**, enter revision feedback via **Reject / Revise**, or attach ultra-high-bitrate **Veo 3.1 4K** renders.\n\n- **Bottom Telemetry Status Bar**:\n  - **Left**: `Today: 3 videos posted`\n  - **Center**: `\360\237\221\201 12.4K views`\n  - **Right**: `$1.20 spent | Budget: $10.00/day`"
    thinking: "**Verifying User Requirements**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the core functions, `compile_applet` and `lint_applet`, have passed without issue! Now, I\'m focusing on ensuring all the user\'s requirements are captured accurately. This involves reviewing the prompt again to confirm the desired front-end aesthetic (n8n dashboard-like or related ideas) is fully understood.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Specifications**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the UI details, starting with the provided screenshot. I\'ve broken down the top bar elements: the layout grid, the Zap badge, the navigation tabs (Pipeline, Analytics, Style Guides, Telegram HITL, and Codebase), the connectivity indicator, settings, the moon icon, and the new job button. The left sidebar\'s \"AGENTS\" section is next, covering the agent header and all nine agents listed, including their functions, descriptions, and models.\n\n\n**Detailing Node Attributes**\n\nI\'m now detailing each node\'s properties. I have descriptions and models (`gemini-3.6-flash`, `postiz-api`), and the status dots (green, amber, gray). My focus is now on mapping the click interaction to canvas focus and selection for each agent. The node arrangements follow a 3-row serpentine pattern. The node styles will have connection handles, icons, labels, and status dots. I am visualizing the SVG wires.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have re-architected the frontend into a **node-based workflow canvas dashboard**, matching the layout, visual structure, and interactive flow:\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural & Visual Implementations\n\n- **Top Navigation Bar**:\n  - **Brand & Menu**: Integrated the 4-square grid app drawer trigger alongside the green electric bolt badge and uppercase `CONTENT-FACTORY` branding.\n  - **Pill Navigation Tabs**: Replaced the previous layout with the centralized n8n pill tabs (**Pipeline**, **Analytics**, **Style Guides**, **Telegram HITL**, and **Codebase**).\n  - **Live Indicator & Controls**: Embedded the `\342\227\217 Connected` green pill indicator, quick settings drawer, dark mode toggle, and a **+ New Job** pipeline creator.\n\n- **Left Sidebar (\"AGENTS\")**:\n  - **Agent Fleet Dossiers**: Styled all 9 autonomous agents (**Manager**, **Researcher**, **Scriptwriter**, **Style Analyst**, **Art Director**, **Video Editor**, **Quality Control**, **Poster**, and **Analyst**) in collapsible cards.\n  - **Sub-Roles & Engine Badges**: Each agent displays their specific division (`ORCHESTRATION`, `RESEARCH OPS`, `CREATIVE`, `VISUAL INTEL`, `ASSEMBLY`, `AUDIT & SAFETY`, `DISTRIBUTION`, `PERFORMANCE`), status dots, and assigned engine badges (`gemini-3.6-flash`, `gemini-3.6-pro`, `ffmpeg + veo`, `postiz-api`).\n  - **Interactive Node Focusing**: Clicking any agent in the sidebar immediately centers and selects the corresponding stage on the canvas.\n\n- **Serpentine Workflow Canvas (11 Interactive Nodes)**:\n  - **Dot Matrix Grid Canvas**: Implemented a deep `#0a0f1d` canvas with custom 24px dot-matrix background styling.\n  - **Geometric 3-Row Node Layout**:\n    - **Row 1 (Left \342\236\224 Right)**: `IDEA` \342\236\224 `RESEARCH` \342\236\224 `SCRIPT` \342\236\224 `QC1`\n    - **Row 2 (Right \360\237\240\224 Left)**: `STYLE` \360\237\240\224 `ART` \360\237\240\224 `VIDEO` \360\237\240\224 `AWAITING_PREMIUM`\n    - **Row 3 (Left \342\236\224 Right)**: `QC2` \342\236\224 `POST` \342\236\224 `ANALYZE`\n  - **Node Aesthetics**: Each node is enclosed in a dark slate container with 4 border connection handles (top, bottom, left, right), an upper-right status dot, large centered stage icons, and stage titles.\n  - **Dynamic SVG Connection Cables**:\n    - **Completed Connections**: Glowing emerald wires (`#10b981`).\n    - **Active Execution Connection**: Amber wire (`#f59e0b`) featuring an animated SVG particle moving along the path.\n    - **Pending Connections**: Dark slate wires (`#283952`).\n  - **Pan & Zoom Interaction**: Full drag-to-pan canvas navigation, zoom in (`+`), zoom out (`\342\210\222`), reset to fit (`\342\233\266`), and canvas lock (`\360\237\224\222`).\n  - **Bottom-Right Mini-Map**: Embedded an interactive mini-map with active viewport bounds tracking and the watermark badge.\n\n- **Right Slide-Out Node Inspector**:\n  - Clicking any node opens a slide-out drawer displaying the stage\'s real-time output payload, token counts, engine details, and execution triggers.\n  - **HITL Gate Controls**: For approval gates (`SCRIPT`, `QC1`, `AWAITING_PREMIUM`, `QC2`), users can directly trigger **Approve Gate**, enter revision feedback via **Reject / Revise**, or attach ultra-high-bitrate **Veo 3.1 4K** renders.\n\n- **Bottom Telemetry Status Bar**:\n  - **Left**: `Today: 3 videos posted`\n  - **Center**: `\360\237\221\201 12.4K views`\n  - **Right**: `$1.20 spent | Budget: $10.00/day`"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 390129029
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
