    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Input**\n\nI\'m focusing on the user\'s image and instructions, striving to grasp the desired \"broad\" style for implementation details. I need to distill the essence of the picture to create a usable reference. I have a clearer idea now.\n\n\n**Refining Functionality Goals**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core functionality, ensuring the backend functions reflect intended purpose and incorporate relevant components from existing builds to display authentic data, not simulated. The image provides excellent insights, which clarify architectural necessities, specifically the multi-agent workflow and the key roles of various agents. The structure of data flows is now much clearer in my mind.\n\n\n**Defining Agent Parameters**\n\nI\'m solidifying the specific roles and capabilities of each sub-agent. The core model will be `gemini-3.6-flash` due to its speed and cost-effectiveness, and I\'m designing a strategy engine for system prompts. I\'m choosing a SQLite database for memory and considering agent clusters. The sub-agents are becoming clear; research agents will use various APIs, like YouTube and web search, while scriptwriting agents will work with `gemini`.\n\n\n**Specifying Sub-Agents**\n\nI\'m now detailing the specific sub-agents and their tools. The scriptwriting agent is designed with tools such as \"Hook Formulas Vault\", \"3-Act Retention Framework\", and \"Character Bible Persona\". Also, the Visual & Art agent will use `gemini-3.7-flash` for creative reasoning and `gemini-2.5-pro` for visual analysis, along with the Pexels API, ComfyUI, and Google Veo. Finally, the Video & Audio Assembly Engine will use `gemini-2.5-pro` and tools like Edge-TTS and FFmpeg. The Quality Control agent utilizes `gemini-3.6-flash`.\n\n\n**Defining Distribution & Metrics**\n\nI\'m now integrating tools for social media distribution and performance analysis. I\'ve added a social distribution agent using Postiz for scheduled cross-platform posting. The performance analytics agent leverages YouTube metrics and an algorithmic feedback loop, feeding insights back into the SQLite vault. I\'m noting the LUFS loudness and AV sync requirements. I\'m also planning the telegram bot integration.\n\n\n**Visualizing Real-Time N8N**\n\nI\'m now focused on the visual interface, specifically how to represent real backend functionality within the N8N-like design. I\'m prioritizing the detailed node representation, especially the AI Agent node, with connections to sub-agents and tools. The node details panel is the real focus, which is essential to provide authentic backend data and functionalities in a testing environment. I\'m keen on integrating a \"Test step\" button that links to real backend endpoints.\n\n\n**Implementing Backend APIs**\n\nI am now structuring the `/server.ts` endpoints to support real data integration. I will build endpoints for real Gemini API execution, incorporating `@google/genai` when `GEMINI_API_KEY` is available, with graceful fallback if the key is missing, pointing to resources to obtain one. Furthermore, I will create real free-tier tool execution endpoints, including YouTube Data API searches, Tavily API searches, and Pexels API queries, with appropriate fallback mechanisms in place when API keys are not configured.\n\n\n"
