  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visuals and Text**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics. I\'ve got two images and the reference text. The focus is now to carefully analyze the visual structure from `Build powerful AI systems fast`. I\'m going to look for visual cues and how they are related to the text provided.\n\n\n**Exploring Workflow Architectures**\n\nI\'m now deep in the workflow, specifically the AI agent\'s structure. It is now focused on the nodes: \'Researcher\', \'Scriptwriter\', and a few others. These sub-agents are integrated, each one with dedicated models and tools. The system employs diverse APIs for its content generation: \'YouTube Data API v3\', \'Tavily Search\', \'SerpAPI\', etc. I\'m focusing on the integration of model pins and system reasoning components.\n\n\n**Dissecting Agent Roles**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific agents within the content generation system. I\'m focusing on the \'Art Director\', \'Video Editor\', \'Quality Control\', \'Distribution\', and \'Analytics\' agents. These have their specific models and tools, such as Gemini models and APIs for video editing and distribution. The structure allows for a sophisticated workflow. I\'m looking at how each component feeds into the next, and how the models\' outputs are integrated for a seamless experience. The visual style uses a red n8n logo with a back arrow and workflow name.\n\n\n**Examining User Interface Components**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI components of the free-tier media pipeline. I\'m focusing on the toggle switches, share buttons, saved statuses, and history icons, and how they contribute to user experience. The left navigation dock with its overview, templates, variables, and help sections are being analyzed in detail. The canvas layout, with its dot grid, zoom controls, and chat button, helps in understanding the user workflow.\n\n\n**Investigating Node Interactions**\n\nI\'m now studying the connections between the nodes. The visual cues with their input and output ports are coming into focus, particularly how they\'re interconnected with connector wires. The sub-ports on the AI Agent, like \'Chat Model\', \'Memory\', and \'Tool\', use bezier spline lines to link to sub-agent pods. Dynamic connection line animations are used to visualize workflow activity. This is leading to the interactive node modal and the official n8n Node Inspector & Execution Panel.\n\n\n**Evaluating Execution Systems**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the system\'s execution aspects. I\'ve focused on the live execution features and the \"Test step\" functionality, which leverages the backend call to `/api/tools/test-node` to provide real-time outputs. These outputs include JSON data, schemas, and previews, like audio players for Edge-TTS, video previews for Pexels, and trend data for YouTube. I\'m also examining the executions tab, with its table displaying execution IDs, statuses, triggers, and durations.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 974473313
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
