  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve begun building out the API in `server.ts`. Currently, I\'m focusing on adding endpoints, specifically `/api/workflow/spec`. This endpoint will return the complete n8n workflow graph specification, including node definitions, connections, and category information.\n\n\n**Expanding API Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now expanding the API endpoints based on the \"Build powerful AI systems fast with n8n!\" guide, focusing on free-tier limits and configuration schemas. I\'ve added `/api/workflow/executions` to display real workflow execution data, and `/api/workflow/run` to trigger live multi-agent workflow executions for different niches. Plus, there\'s `/api/tools/execute-node` for testing individual nodes.\n\n\n**Testing New Node Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now testing new node capabilities. I\'ve successfully tested `pexels-api`, `edge-tts`, and `ffmpeg` to confirm they return real stock clips, speech data, and video commands. Also, testing `postiz`, `telegram-trigger`, and `sqlite-vault` is in progress. Finally, I\'ve added a `/api/free-tier-reference` endpoint for cross-referencing limits and model details in the UI. I am defining `WorkflowNode` types in `src/types.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining Workflow Objects**\n\nI\'m now defining critical data structures. I\'ve outlined `WorkflowEdge` objects with properties such as ID, connection details, style, animation, and status. Furthermore, I\'ve defined `WorkflowExecution` to track workflow runs, including status, timing data, node execution details, and logs. Finally, `FreeTierModelRef` is in progress, for cross-referencing model details and limits.\n\n\n**Visualizing The Workflow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the canvas view and overall node layout. I\'m incorporating a dot grid for style, mirroring n8n\'s tool rail. I\'ve added a zoom toolbar, and a central \"Execute Workflow\" button with running state and a \"Test Agent Chat\" drawer. A mini-map and free-tier budget meter are planned. Also, I\'ve outlined the broad node topology, with the Telegram trigger leading into switch branches for voice and text, eventually converging at an AI agent that handles the orchestration.\n\n\n**Orchestrating AI Agents**\n\nI\'m now deep in architecting the AI agent orchestration. I\'m focusing on the `Telegram Response Dispatcher`, the `SQLite Vault` database append, and data cleanup processes. Error handling is critical, so I\'m also building a `Telegram Error Alert & Retry Handler` in parallel. I\'m also branching out Sub-Agent Pods & Tools.\n\n\n**Defining Sub-Agent Clusters**\n\nI\'m now outlining a series of sub-agent clusters to manage different aspects of video creation. Cluster 4 focuses on video editing using the `Video Editor Agent` along with tools like `Edge-TTS` and `FFmpeg`. I\'ve defined the `Art Director & Style Agent` and other agents for the sub-agent pods. There are also nodes for social distribution and quality control.\n\n\n**Designing Node Inspection**\n\nI\'m now creating an authentic n8n node inspector modal. This includes displaying node details like name, type, and API key status, alongside a free-tier limits badge for quick reference. I\'m also implementing a parameter editor, a test/execute node button for real-time results, and input/output data tabs for comprehensive viewing of execution results. I\'m building this view into an executions view that\'s useful for debugging.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 89148545
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
