  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the API endpoints needed for real data and backend execution. Specifically, I\'m designing the tools execution and workflow endpoints for `server.ts`. I\'ve outlined the `/api/free-tier-reference` endpoint, which will return structured metadata based on user reference, specifying `gemini-3` for LLM & Vision.\n\n\n**Expanding API Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of API functions like `/api/workflow/spec`, which returns a node graph. I am integrating diverse tools: YouTube Data API v3, Tavily Search, Pexels API, Edge-TTS, FFmpeg, Postiz, a Telegram Bot, and SQLite. The goal is to build a robust system that accounts for various inputs and outputs, and this is now being reflected in the endpoints. Key environment variables will be checked for correct configuration.\n\n\n**Mapping Agent Flows**\n\nI am currently working on connecting sub-agents and tools through bottom subpins. I\'m focusing on defining the connections for agents like \"Researcher Agent,\" \"Scriptwriter Agent,\" and \"Art & Style Agent.\" I\'ve connected these agents to tools such as \"YouTube Data API v3,\" \"Tavily Search,\" \"SerpAPI,\" \"Firecrawl,\" \"Jina AI Reader,\" \"Hook Formulas Vault,\" \"3-Act Retention Loop,\" \"Character Persona Injector,\" \"Pexels Stock API,\" and \"ComfyUI Local.\"\n\n\n**Connecting Agent Nodes**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the connections between sub-agents and their corresponding tools within the new Veo 3.1 prompt pack. Specifically, I\'ve mapped out the tools for the \"Video Editor Agent,\" \"Quality Control Agent,\" \"Poster Agent,\" and \"Analyst Agent\" pods, each leveraging different Gemini models and specialized tools. I\'m also planning the `/api/workflow/executions` endpoint to display recent, realistic execution runs, and I\'ll detail the `/api/workflow/run` endpoint for end-to-end execution.\n\n\n**Designing Execution Steps**\n\nI\'m now outlining a complete multi-agent pipeline and how its execution will work. This involves handling a niche, format, platform selection, premium options, and simulated errors. I\'m detailing the real execution steps, like formatting a Telegram trigger, the AI Agent\'s decomposition of the task, the Researcher\'s trend search, and Scriptwriter\'s retention script. Each node, such as YT and Tavily, will have real execution pathways. Crucially, I\'m integrating data validation and error handling at each phase, including generating execution logs and a step-by-step trace with real data for user feedback. I\'m working on `/api/tools/execute-node` to allow testing nodes with custom params and returning real data.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 890398260
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
