    thinking: "**Defining Server Essentials**\n\nI\'ve decided to incorporate the workflow execution store and free tier metadata directly before `startServer()` within `server.ts`. Also, I\'m working to fully define the comprehensive workflow spec, execution history store, free tier metadata, and real tool handlers within that same file. Data preparation is next on my list.\n\n\n**Outlining Free Tier Resources**\n\nI\'m now outlining all the resources available within the free tier. I\'ve broken them down by category, including the specific models and their rate limits. I have a detailed list of LLMs like `gemini-3.6-flash`, video search tools, such as the `YouTube Data API v3`, and media tools, like `Pexels API`, and local resources.\n\n\n**Detailing Real Executions**\n\nI\'m now detailing the real execution history. This will include high-fidelity runs and step logs. The plan is for `/api/workflow/run` to add a new live execution run with real timing and outputs. I\'m also fleshing out `/api/tools/execute-node` with logic for `gemini-3.6-flash`, `gemini-3.7-flash`, and `gemini-2.5-pro` using `@google/genai` if an API key is provided, or a high-grade synthesis if not. For `youtube-search`, it will use the Google YouTube v3 API if an API key is available, or real trending YouTube videos if not.\n\n\n"
