  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Previous State**\n\nOkay, so I see it. The old version of `N8nWorkflowCanvas.tsx` was simpler, a basic grid arrangement of rectangular boxes \342\200\223 a snake grid of 10 nodes for the workflow, each representing a stage. Specifically: IDEA, RESEARCH, SCRIPT, QC1, STYLE, ART, VIDEO, QC2, POST, ANALYZE.\n\n\n**Reimagining the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual redesign, drawing inspiration from the provided n8n image. I\'m prioritizing a top bar with key elements: the n8n logo, workflow title, badges, active toggle, share button, save indicator, and a Github star. The mode switcher pills (Editor, Execute, Settings) will also be included. The key is to capture its overall look and feel, incorporating current functionalities.\n\n\n**Developing the Next Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the supporting UI elements. The \"Executions\" panel will show a history table with real-time run data. I\'m also working on the \"Free Tier Stack\" display, a reference matrix. The left dock is also getting attention, with a vertical rail of n8n icons. The canvas itself needs a full authentic n8n visual style. Dark dot matrix background, node cards with input/output ports. The **AI Agent** card specifically includes some sub-pin connection ports.\n\n\n**Designing the Connectors**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual flow. I\'m imagining spline bezier connector wires weaving between nodes and sub-agent clusters to represent data flow. These will have pulsing animated execution dots to track active wires when a pipeline is running, offering dynamic visual feedback. I\342\200\231m thinking about the floating toolbar, with zoom controls, an \"Execute Workflow\" button, and a \"Test Agent Chat\" feature.\n\n\n\n**Implementing the Output View**\n\nI\'m now deep in the details of the \"Test Step\" functionality. I\'m focusing on making that \"Execute Node\" button functional, actually calling the backend. I\'m prioritizing displaying the real output, formatted and interactive, complete with copy buttons for quick access. This includes providing the outputs for each service.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
