    thinking: "**Exploring Tab Options**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently assessing the possibilities for tabs within `Header.tsx`. I\'m leaning toward including \"Workflow Editor\" for the n8n canvas, \"Executions\" for history and step runs, and the \"Free Tier Stack,\" drawn from the user\'s input. The \"Vault\" tab is still under consideration, however.\n\n\n**Analyzing Vault Storage**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the \"Vault Storage\" component. I\'m thinking of creating storage for 13 different models. I\'m thinking of building out some hooks, style guides, and logs. This will need to be well-structured. I have also decided on including a \"Telegram HITL\" interactive simulator and \"Project Files\" for the code. I am also planning on what `N8nWorkflowCanvas.tsx` will deliver.\n\n\n**Defining Sub-Agent Roles**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the roles for each sub-agent pod. This involves assigning specific tools and models: Tavily, Firecrawl, and Jina Reader. The scriptwriter is now in charge of the `Hook Formulas Vault` and `Character Bible`. The Art & Style Agent will be responsible for `gemini-3.7-flash (Creative)`, `Pexels API (20k/mo)`, and `Veo 3.1 Prompt Pack ($20 manual)`.\n\n\n**Refining UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the UI. I have added \"Execute Step / Test Node\" functionality and I\'m targeting rich visual results. I\'m also adding primary actions at the bottom center, particularly an \"Execute Workflow\" button for the multi-agent execution pipeline, and a \"Test Agent Chat\" prompt drawer. There will also be a Quick Mode toggle in the canvas header. I\'m looking into how to modularize the files, especially around `N8nWorkflowCanvas.tsx` and adding `FreeTierReferenceModal`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 405855049
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
