  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyze User Feedback**\n\nI\'ve been carefully reviewing the user\'s feedback and the visuals. My current focus is dissecting the user\'s desire for a hovering or tap-and-reveal interaction. I am now concentrating on the spacing and positioning of the elements, striving to discern their specific expectations. I believe I am close to determining the ideal layout.\n\n\n**Examine Visual Layout**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to the videos, specifically the layout. Video 1 demonstrates a clear horizontal node arrangement, and generous spacing is provided between these nodes. This is an important detail! In the video, the workflow is triggered when \"execute workflow\" is pressed. The details of the node arrangement are clear. Now I am carefully analyzing the interactive bottom panel/dock, and how it is employed.\n\n\n**Detail Workflow Execution**\n\nI\'ve been examining the workflow execution details. I\'m noting the speed of each stage: AI agent, model calls, image generation, video rendering, and uploads. The success messages and timing are incredibly useful. The bottom panel\'s design, displaying node names, success badges, and data previews, is clear.\n\n\n**Detail Node Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of each node\'s data. For the AI agent, I\'m noting the prompt and output format. The voice generator, image generator, video renderer, and uploader - each component has unique details: audio player, preview, URLs, video thumbnails, upload statuses, and links. I am noting how the bottom dock is used in Video 2! It has both \"Chat\" and \"Logs\" functions. I\'m focusing on the canvas interaction, too.\n\n\n**Refine Node Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how nodes interact. The user wants highlights with a glow, plus a hover tooltip/card or bottom inspector to show inputs, outputs, and functionality. Clicking should open the output in the bottom inspector. Node spacing is also crucial, with horizontal gaps around 120-160px and vertical sub-nodes having 100px+ gaps. I am going to examine `N8nWorkflowCanvas.tsx` to understand the current structure!\n\n\n**Clarify Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics of the interactive elements. I am visualizing the implementation of the user\'s \"hovering or tap-then-under\" concept. I see the bottom dock as key. I\'m noting that tapping a node, or clicking it in the execution timeline, will select that node for inspection. The logs will be displayed in one area, and the node\'s functionality and data in another, below.\n\n\n**Detail Hover Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive elements, specifically the hover states. I envision a floating tooltip revealing the node\'s function and real-time data, with a \"tap to view\" action. Clicking or tapping a node will open the bottom panel immediately, for further inspection. The design will include an \"Execute workflow\" button and workflow run indicators. I am also examining the current node structure.\n\n\n**Examine Node Positioning**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the node coordinates within `server.ts`. I see the `x` and `y` values define the positions, revealing the close proximity of specific nodes like the \"Trigger\" and \"Switch,\" each positioned with a separation of approximately 180px, closely stacked in horizontal alignment. I am noting the detailed positioning of all nodes, and am considering the implications of this layout on user experience and the overall workflow, while considering all the prior details.\n\n\n**Assess Node Proximity**\n\nI am now assessing the spatial arrangement of the nodes. I see overlapping or minimal separation, as little as 20-40 pixels, is causing visual clutter. I\'m noting the clear flow in Video 1, triggered by \"Execute workflow\" or the Telegram Trigger, and its sequential steps. I\'m focusing on the branching and recombining, followed by video rendering, review, download, and upload, as well as the modular layout.\n\n\n\n**Adjust Node Spacing**\n\nI\'m now revising node spacing, aiming for clear separation. The user\'s feedback makes it clear; I\'m implementing substantial horizontal gaps of 260px-320px and 140px-180px vertical spacing. This will greatly enhance visibility of connecting elements. I am now considering how the hover and tap interactions will be implemented with these changes.\n\n\n**Implement Dock Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new bottom dock interactions. It will mirror Videos 1 and 2, acting as a logs sidebar on the left. This sidebar will list workflow nodes with real-time execution statuses and quick timing data. Selecting a node highlights it on the canvas and displays its full details on the right side of the dock. The dock will have a resizable/collapsible height, and will be between 280-360px.\n\n\n**Detail Node Content**\n\nI am now focusing on the right side of the dock, where I\'ll render node functionality and data. I\'m imagining a header with node name, execution time, and output/input tabs. I need to include interactive visual content tailored to each node type: an audio player for voice nodes, a script display for prompts, a video preview for image and video nodes, and a YouTube publishing card for upload nodes.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 340187157
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
