ideo 2.\n\nI\'m also spacing and organizing workflow nodes for improved navigation. I\'m placing the `node-trigger` at x: 100, y: 220, `node-edit-fields` at x: 380, y: 220, and the `node-ai-agent` at x: 680, y: 190. Sub-agent nodes are being positioned underneath.\n\n\n**Organizing Visual Flow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on arranging the remaining workflow nodes. I\'ve placed `node-json-split` and the two subsequent branches (audio/voice and visuals/stock) at their respective coordinates. The merge, render, wait, download, and upload nodes are also positioned. I\'m also implementing the Research Pod, connected from the AI Agent, with sub-nodes for YouTube Trend Intel and data API interaction.\n\n\n**Optimizing Node Connectivity**\n\nI\'ve just finished placing the remaining nodes for the Distribution & Feedback Pod, ensuring ample horizontal space for clean wire connections; each now has 260-300px. I\'ve also verified a default zoom setting and pan/focus functionality, and I\'m very happy with how the layout looks.\n\nNow, I\'m examining the design of the bottom dock, which will be the functionality viewer *under* the canvas. I\'m focusing on incorporating a resizable drawer with \"Logs,\" \"Output,\" and \"Input\" panels, similar to the examples from Video 1 and Video 2, with key features like node run items and interactive canvas highlighting.\n\n\n**Designing Node Functionality**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on the new sub-panel. It will feature a tab bar with the node\'s name and execution details, alongside active \"Output\" and \"Input\" buttons. I\'ll include item count pills, view toggles for \"Formatted View,\" \"Raw JSON,\" and \"Table,\" and action buttons for download, copy, and execution. The panel will also be a rich visualization for node functionality, including all data types. I\'m prioritizing the chat trigger tab, too.\n\n\n"
