  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Integration**\n\nOkay, I\'ve examined `NodeInspectorModal.tsx` and now I\'m comparing it to the user\'s video. It seems the key difference is in how it\'s integrated with the canvas; in the video, it\'s a bottom drawer rather than a popup. The current implementation doesn\'t align with the video\'s layout which appears integrated beneath the canvas, offering a tighter visual structure.\n\n\n**Investigating Layout Options**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating a bottom dock for the inspector, similar to n8n\'s design. The user\'s video highlights the need for instant previews and a bottom panel that updates dynamically with node information. To achieve this, I\'m considering a dedicated `N8nBottomDock.tsx` component or direct integration with `N8nWorkflowCanvas.tsx` or `App.tsx`. The goal is to ensure smooth interactions for hover and click events. I need to make the canvas the top level so that the dock is under the canvas.\n\n\n**Designing Bottom Dock Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the bottom dock\'s structure. It should be resizable (collapsed to expanded, closeable), featuring two left-side tabs: \"Logs\" (execution steps with canvas focus) and \"Chat\" (interactive prompting and real-time steps). The right side will display the node functionality viewer, complete with execution status, \"OUTPUT/INPUT\" tabs, view switches, action buttons, and type-specific preview content, like an interactive audio player for voice nodes.\n\n\n**Visualizing Content Workflow**\n\nI\'m now putting together the workflow\'s visual presentation. I\'m focusing on rendering a final video, designing a YouTube Shorts card, outlining an AI agent\'s role, setting up an image prompt generator, and integrating stock video clips from Pexels. The core concept is creating a system for generating short-form video. I need to make all of the relevant components play a role.\n\n\n**Defining Data Pipelines**\n\nI\'m now outlining data pipelines, considering competitor benchmarks (titles, views, retention), input formatting (niche, duration, platform), and the trigger mechanism (timestamp). Next, I\'ll tackle merge streams with a visualizer to sync audio and video cuts. Finally, I\'ll structure the downloadable asset package with the master video, audio, subtitles, and production manifest. The JSON output view will be formatted to match n8n.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 26
      nanos: 361184480
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
