    thinking: "**Analyzing Types and Components**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the types in `src/types.ts` are set. Now, I\'m focusing on creating `N8nBottomDock.tsx` and integrating it with `N8nWorkflowCanvas.tsx`. My current focus is on what data the `N8nBottomDock.tsx` component should accept, specifically the `selectedNode` input.\n\n\n**Defining Bottom Dock Specs**\n\nI\'m now detailing the `N8nBottomDock`\'s functionality. The top dock bar\'s design includes tab switching for logs and a chat trigger, with node info display including icon, name, and execution status. Quick action buttons like Execute Node and Copy JSON are planned, along with dock size controls. I\'m focusing on UI interactions next.\n\n\n**Detailing UI Specifications**\n\nI\'m now detailing the UI within the bottom dock. For the \"Logs\" tab, I\'m structuring a scrollable list of executed pipeline nodes with icons, names, and durations, and making it so clicking a step selects the node for rich functionality on the right. If the tab is on \"Chat Trigger\", an interactive panel shows message history and handles the \"Send\" button to trigger the workflow with a user prompt. In the right area/OUTPUT tab, I have designed a formatted view that corresponds to node category/type. For \"Voice Generator\", for example, this will include an audio playback bar.\n\n\n**Rendering Video & Upload**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the final output stage now. I\'ve designed the video preview card with a 9:16 vertical ratio video player, which contains the duration and an FPS badge. This will also have captions, and a download button that triggers a real download. Finally, I\'ve designed the YouTube Shorts preview card with the channel and status information.\n\n\n**Designing Shorts UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the UI for YouTube Shorts. The design includes a preview card with description and hashtags. It also provides \"Direct Open in YouTube\" and \"Copy Link\" buttons. I\'ve designed sections for AI Agent and Image Prompt generation, including the director reasoning box with directives, the viral 3-Act Structure, target audience profile, and token efficiency for the AI agent. The image prompt generator provides storyboard prompts for the four shots with detailed descriptions for each.\n\n\n**Generating Assets**\n\nI\'m now generating assets. There are 4 portrait vertical video clips with video thumbnails with hover play effect. Each has a clip title, duration (8.5s), resolution (1080x1920), photographer credit, a royalty-free license note, and a download clip button. I am also researching the YouTube Data API v3 and benchmarking top 2 viral competitors with view counts (1.8M views, 940K views) and retention rates (86% avg retention), with a virality score meter of 93.8/100. I have implemented a clean parameter table with fields for Niche, target duration, format, and destination platforms. Lastly, I\'m working on the audio & visual synchronization matrix which shows the voice track aligned with 4 cut timestamps, and creating file download links for Master Video (.mp4), Voice Track (.mp3), Burned Subtitles (.srt), and Manifest (.json).\n\n\n**Refining Data Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on enhanced output visualization. I\'m prioritizing a formatted, syntax-highlighted JSON tree within the OUTPUT tab, complete with line numbers, expand/collapse functionality, and a \'Copy JSON\' button. I\'m working on the INPUT tab, specifically, to show the upstream input parameters that triggered each node. I\'m also refining hover states in the `N8nWorkflowCanvas.tsx` to enhance node details. I\'m planning to make an interactive display of waveforms for audio and the video player\'s controls using HTML5 tags.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 37
      nanos: 724439620
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
